# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM Market News Sentiment Digest — environment variables for the Vue app
# Copy this file to .env (never commit .env) and fill in the values.
# Restart `npm run dev` after changing it. Vite only exposes variables that
# start with VITE_, and everything exposed ends up in the browser bundle.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase project URL.
# Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > Data API (or API) > Project URL.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Public client key: the "anon" key (legacy JWT, starts with eyJ...) or the newer
# "publishable" key (starts with sb_publishable_...). Both act as the `anon` role.
# Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API Keys (or the "Connect" button).
# You may name this variable VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY instead; the app accepts either.
# Safe in the browser ONLY because Row Level Security + column grants in
# supabase/schema.sql limit what it can do.
# NEVER put the service_role / secret key here: that key belongs in the Make.com
# Supabase connection only.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key

# Not variables of this app (they live in Make.com connections, never in the repo):
# - Supabase service_role / secret key  -> Make > Connections > Supabase
# - Gemini API key (Google AI Studio)    -> Make > Connections > Google Gemini AI
# - Make webhook URL                     -> Supabase > Database > Webhooks
